Strongtalk (Rust and WebAssembly edition)

Strongtalk was created by Animorphic Systems (LongView Technologies) and released
as open source by Sun Microsystems in 2006 under the BSD 3-Clause license in
LICENSE. This edition
re-implements it in Rust; it keeps Sun's license and notice because it was made by
studying the original Strongtalk system.

Parts of this repository that are entirely new work and contain nothing derived
from Sun's Strongtalk may also be used under the Zero-Clause BSD license, which
asks for nothing at all: see LICENSE-0BSD for the list.

The program includes open-source Rust libraries under their own permissive
licenses (MIT / Apache-2.0); see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
